WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.760
From a veteran with a 50-year career to a former&nbsp;
pro wrestler to a few just getting their start,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.456
these are the "Walking Dead"&nbsp;
actors we've lost over the years.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.120
According to the New York Times, Scott&nbsp;
Wilson's breakout role was in the 1967 film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.640
"In Cold Blood," based on the&nbsp;
Truman Capote novel. From there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.640
he went on to star in 80 films and&nbsp;
television shows throughout his career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.600
Wilson joined the cast of "The&nbsp;
Walking Dead" in season two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.880
where he played farmer Hershel Greene, who let&nbsp;
the group of survivors take refuge on his farm.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.440
The character, with his strong moral compass,&nbsp;
was a welcome addition to the show and a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.440
foil for Rick Grimes. Hershel survived&nbsp;
until halfway through the fourth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.880
when he became a victim of the sadistic Governor.&nbsp;
Wilson did film a guest appearance which aired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:51.360
in season nine after his real-life death in&nbsp;
October 2018. He died of cancer at the age of 76,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.220
but his last scenes provided a fitting&nbsp;
tribute to both the man and the character.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.560
"I know it's been hard."

00:01:00.508 --> 00:01:01.228
"It has."

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.040
Russell Comegys was no stranger to the&nbsp;
industry when he was cast in his very brief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.080
role in "The Walking Dead." He has made many&nbsp;
appearances in films, such as "The Lucky One"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.960
and the 2004 version of "The Punisher,"&nbsp;
and shows such as "The Vampire Diaries."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.600
Unfortunately, his career was cut short.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.480
He was in a third-season episode of "The Walking&nbsp;
Dead," playing a hitchhiker. When Rick, Carl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:30.240
and Michonne drive to retrieve more weapons, they&nbsp;
pass a man, played by Comegys, on the road. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.120
speed past him, despite his pleas that they stop.&nbsp;
This scene demonstrates that the survivor group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:41.280
couldn't risk taking on anyone new. The promising&nbsp;
actor died at the age of 45 in 2017 when,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:47.705
according to news station WTOC, he and another&nbsp;
person were killed in a rollover car accident.

00:01:48.253 --> 00:01:52.160
Dango Nguyen was just getting started&nbsp;
in his acting career when he appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:56.480
on "The Walking Dead." With two TV&nbsp;
episodes and one film to his credit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.320
Nguyen appeared in seven episodes of&nbsp;
the third season of "The Walking Dead."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:05.840
Acting was his third career after professional&nbsp;
wrestling and almost 20 years as a firefighter.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.800
Athens-Clarke County Fire and Emergency Services&nbsp;
announced his death on its Facebook page.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.920
Nguyen died at age 48 from cancer in&nbsp;
2019. He played a bodyguard of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:20.800
Governor and clashed with Rick's group in&nbsp;
Woodbury. His experience led him to parts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.600
in "The Originals" and "MacGyver," and he also&nbsp;
completed stunts in several films and movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.264
including "Mile 22," "NCIS:&nbsp;
New Orleans," and "Insatiable."

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.600
"The Walking Dead" was Rodney M. Hall's&nbsp;
first-ever credit according to IMDb.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.160
Hall appeared in the second episode of the&nbsp;
first season of "The Walking Dead" as a walker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:45.040
The episode featured Rick and Glenn slathering&nbsp;
guts all over themselves to get through a crowd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.920
of walkers, Hall included. It is difficult&nbsp;
to pick him out of this large undead crowd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.400
but he did complete a few other&nbsp;
appearances before his death in 2021.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.280
Hall also had parts in "Franklin &amp; Bash,"&nbsp;
"Drop Dead Diva," "The Underlying," and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.640
"Devil's Knot." Not much is known&nbsp;
about his life between his last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:07.920
screen appearance in 2013 and his death&nbsp;
at age 50 from an apparent drug overdose.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.854
His memorial announcement requested&nbsp;
donations to drug and alcohol facilities.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:18.640
Moses J. Moseley was 31 at the time of his&nbsp;
death. His roles were mostly uncredited before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:23.200
appearing on "The Walking Dead," but one of&nbsp;
them was for "The Hunger Games: Catching Fire."

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.360
His real claim to fame came when he was in&nbsp;
six episodes throughout the early seasons of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:31.840
"The Walking Dead." Moseley played Mike, who&nbsp;
was one of Michonne's jawless pet zombies.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.280
"I made it so they couldn't&nbsp;
bite. Couldn't scratch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.280
I tied chains around their necks. It was insane."

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.800
After the show, he appeared in guest roles on&nbsp;
several other shows. He died from a gunshot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:51.280
wound to the head in January 2022. According to&nbsp;
Today, his autopsy was not conclusive. This makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.560
his manner of death still unconfirmed, even though&nbsp;
he was found in his car with the gun in his lap.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.640
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal&nbsp;
thoughts, please dial or text 988 to speak with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:09.161
The National Suicide Prevention Lifeline. You&nbsp;
can also seek help by visiting 988lifeline.org.

